lement ANSI color constants for standard file-type colors and a Colorize(text, colorCode string) helper per format PRD\n    - id: R4\n      text: pkg/format must compile with zero external dependencies beyond Go stdlib; module path is github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils\n\n  design_decisions:\n    - id: D1\n      text: \"Each source file is named after its primary exported function group per P7 -- size.go for size formatting, columns.go for column alignment, color.go for ANSI colors -- not after the package name\"\n    - id: D2\n      text: pkg/format uses Go standard library only with no external dependencies per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology_choices\n\n  acceptance_criteria:\n    - id: AC1\n      text: \"go build ./pkg/format/ succeeds on Linux with zero errors\"\n    - id: AC2\n      text: Size formatter returns K/M/G suffixed strings for 1024, 1048576, and 1073741824 byte inputs matching GNU coreutils -h output format\n    - id: AC3\n      text: Column alignment function produces equal-width columns for a representative two-row three-column string table without truncating any cell value\n    - id: AC4\n      text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/ reports no issues\"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15901,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15901},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a0d42e2-bed8-433b-9369-b2c11091d97b","uuid":"ee35273d-546c-47e9-bec3-74a61894ba73"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01UwA4qRmwxtMwgWYuuV3Hh2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` — Go binary per utility, contains implementation + differential tests\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstraction layer\n- `pkg/format/` — Shared output formatting (columns, colors, units)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — Differential testing harness\n- `magefiles/` — Mage build targets (scaffolded; orchestrator boundary)\n- `docs/` — Human-authored specs (PRDs, use cases, test suites)\n\n**Current State**: Working branch is spec-only. Generated code exists at `generation-merged` tags for pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge — but not on the current branch. Issue #282 is in-progress for rel00.0-uc004 (pkg/testutils differential harness).\n\n**Current Release**: rel00.0 — Batch 0, foundational infrastructure.\n- uc001-magefiles: spec_complete, not started\n- uc002-format: spec_complete, not started\n- uc003-sys: spec_complete, not started\n- uc004-testutils: spec_complete, **in progress** (issue #282)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the active release. Three use cases remain unstarted: uc001 (magefiles/cmd/version), uc002 (pkg/format), uc003 (pkg/sys).\n\nPer P8 canonical ordering — libraries before consumers, alphabetical tiebreak: `pkg/format` (f < s) precedes `pkg/sys`, and both precede `cmd/version`. Neither depends on the other; pkg/format uses stdlib only with no pkg/sys dependency. Since the single task budget is exhausted by pkg/format, pkg/sys follows in a subsequent session.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format size, column, and color formatting (rel00.0-uc002)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component description and design_decisions)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read the format PRD -- filename matches prd*-format.yaml)\n      - go.mod (module path -- github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte-size conversion to K/M/G strings\n      - path: pkg/format/columns.go\n        action: create\n        note: Fixed-width column alignment for tabular ls-l style output\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color constants and colorize helper for file types and permission bits\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: >\n          Implement human-readable size formatting that converts an int64 byte count\n          to a K/M/G suffixed string matching GNU coreutils -h output format,\n          per the format PRD requirements\n      - id: R2\n        text: >\n          Implement column alignment that accepts a row-major [][]string table and\n          returns rows padded to uniform per-column widths without truncating any\n          cell, per the format PRD requirements\n      - id: R3\n        text: >\n          Implement ANSI color constants for standard file-type colors and a\n          Colorize(text, colorCode string) string helper that wraps text in ANSI\n          escape sequences, per the format PRD requirements\n      - id: R4\n        text: >\n          pkg/format must compile with zero external dependencies beyond Go stdlib;\n          no cmd/ or other internal packages may be imported; module path is\n          github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils per go.mod\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: >\n          Each source file is named after its primary exported function group per P7\n          naming convention -- size.go for size formatting, columns.go for column\n          alignment, color.go for ANSI colors -- not after the package name\n          (testutils/testutils.go anti-pattern)\n      - id: D2\n        text: >\n          pkg/format uses Go standard library only with no external dependencies\n          per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology_choices; golang.org/x/sys is reserved\n          for pkg/sys only\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./pkg/format/ succeeds on Linux with zero errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: >\n          Size formatter returns correctly suffixed strings (K/M/G) for 1024,\n          1048576, and 1073741824 byte inputs matching GNU coreutils -h output\n          format\n      - id: AC3\n        text: >\n          Column alignment function produces equal-width columns for a\n          representative two-row three-column string table without truncating\n          any cell value\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go vet ./pkg/format/ reports no issues\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15901,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15901},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a0d42e2-bed8-433b-9369-b2c11091d97b","uuid":"91c8a30b-c248-4282-ad53-d9521ebb126b"}
